{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"hypothesis-specific-obstructions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3a21b4e02b3d2d930ab451d425e96d8c6264fdace0f75c4a360ed23d391dbb69/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa","passage_ref":"sha256:d4cff05445a8091e88a0215dc5b8dd28497dfc8c7317357a03f3ed6190b2e19c/papers/long.md/sha256:3a21b4e02b3d2d930ab451d425e96d8c6264fdace0f75c4a360ed23d391dbb69/papers/long.json/passages/hypothesis-specific-obstructions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&paper=long&passage=hypothesis-specific-obstructions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&paper=long&passage=hypothesis-specific-obstructions","span":{"end_byte":420549,"end_line":3870,"start_byte":391783,"start_line":3634},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&view=arguments&node=long.prop-critical-band-index&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&node=long.prop-critical-band-index&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&node=long.prop-critical-band-index&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&view=arguments&node=long.prop-critical-band-index&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&ref=sha256%3Af31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5%2Fnodes%2Flong.prop-critical-band-index","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-critical-band-index"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-critical-band-index"],"id":"long.prop-critical-band-index","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 10.16 (Quantifier collapse: one critical index suffices, not $`d{+}1`$)","locator":"Long record Proposition 10.16, p. 119, label prop:critical-band-index","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $d,E\\in\\mathbb N$ and assume $E\\le2^{d+1}$. Then the purely combinatorial statement $\\mathsf{DyadicBandEscape}(d,E) \\iff \\exists j,\\ \\mathsf{CriticalDyadicBandIndex}(d,E,j)\\land\nE+2(d+j)\\le 2^{d-j+1}$ collapses the $\\forall j\\in[0,d]$ band-avoidance condition (formally $d{+}1$ separate inequalities) to checking exactly *one* nearest-boundary index $j$. The range assumption ensures that a dyadic threshold lies at or above $E$. Choose the smallest such threshold: smaller thresholds are already below $E$, while larger thresholds have narrower forbidden bands. Without the range assumption all bands escape automatically when $E>2^{d+1}$, but no critical index exists; $(d,E)=(0,3)$ is the smallest example. Specialised to the concrete seam reset charge, $\\mathsf{SeamUpperResetCriticalBandEscape}$ is proved logically *equivalent* to Definition 10.15’s hypothesis. Zero Mersenne/seam content in the core lemma ; pure $(d,E,j)$ arithmetic over powers of 2.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-critical-band-index","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-critical-band-index","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-critical-band-index%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_critical_band_index_collapse%22%2C%22formalizes%